Give AudioClipPlayhead::state an explicit initialiser.

Clang (with libstdc++) treats the nested `State` struct as not default-constructible inside its
enclosing class, so `std::atomic<State>` has no default constructor and
`std::make_shared<AudioClipPlayhead>()` fails to compile. An explicit initialiser avoids the
atomic's default constructor. To upstream (tracktion_engine develop).

--- a/modules/tracktion_engine/model/clips/tracktion_AudioClipBase.h
+++ b/modules/tracktion_engine/model/clips/tracktion_AudioClipBase.h
@@ -52,7 +52,7 @@
         uint32_t lastUpdateMs = 0;
     };
 
-    std::atomic<State> state;
+    std::atomic<State> state { State {} };
 };
 
